KG42.register("clusters-e56497a4a65ac56e54fc30d7",{"id":"28-multiclass_prosumer_preferences::v142-d-K002","paper":"28-multiclass_prosumer_preferences","label":"Energy categories, load-use eligibility, and substitution energy-storage authority","record":{"cluster_id":"v142-d-K002","label":"Energy categories, load-use eligibility, and substitution energy-storage authority","market_meaning":"Energy is classified by valuable source attributes; the prosumer's allowed category set limits the scope of load use, and the substitution set limits the authority for category energy to be converted into grid energy storage. Constraints in product definition, consumer eligibility, and welfare configuration jointly express this candidate rule; subsidy eligibility and green energy conditions are limited to the stated case.","mechanism_ids":["v141-a-M01"],"market_types":["LEM"],"process_stages":["participation","clearing"],"scope_disposition":"conditional","scope_explanation":"The general category-set rule and the green and subsidized energy in the case are conditionally corresponding and cannot be directly equated. The load-use set and the substitution energy-storage set have different purposes and remain independent; the existing load formula has not yet explicitly closed the prohibition condition for categories outside the set.","assembly_status":"partial","boundary_rationale":"Product attributes directly affect load allocation and substitution energy storage through category permissions, forming an independent authority rule. R003 only shares the relevant feasibility interface; its bundled clauses cannot be deduplicated as a whole with any single permission.","chain_bindings":[{"chain_id":"v141-c-R010","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Define differentiated energy products and permissions for load, substitution energy storage, and case categories."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R007","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"From the perspective of demand participants, specify allowed categories and case subsidy use eligibility, complementary to product permissions."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R003","ownership":"shared","role":"interface","rationale":"Shares category sets and constraints entering the welfare configuration feasible region, and does not re-assume welfare optimization in this cluster."}],"connections":[{"connection_id":"v142-d-K002-L01","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R010","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R007","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R010::theta::v141-c-R010-p-Ki","v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C002","v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C007"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R007::theta::v141-c-R007-theta-K_i","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C003","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-G01-E20","v141-b-g02-e027"],"rationale":"The product's usable categories and the consumer's allowed set jointly determine the same load permission; subsidy restrictions are two functional perspectives on the same case permission."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K002-L02","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R007","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R007::theta::v141-c-R007-theta-K_i","v141-c-R007::x::v141-c-R007-x-zik","v141-c-R007::x::v141-c-R007-x-zig"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R003::theta::theta_K_i","v141-c-R003::x::var_z_ik","v141-c-R003::x::var_z_ig","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C009"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-G01-E20","v141-b-G01-E30"],"rationale":"The allowed category set and load allocation power are used in the load constraint of the welfare problem, providing a quantity interface from eligibility to allocation; no new graph edge from a participation node to a clearing node is added."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K002-L03","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R010","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R010::theta::v141-c-R010-p-Kg","v141-c-R010::x::v141-c-R010-x-bikg","v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C003","v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C004"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R003::theta::theta_K_g","v141-c-R003::x::var_b_ikg","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C011"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-G01-E24","v141-b-G01-E25","v141-b-G01-E30"],"rationale":"The product chain separately retains in-set permission and out-of-set zeroing, while the welfare chain expresses the two conditions combined; the two jointly correspond to this constraint, and neither individual item is equivalent to the entire constraint."}],"object_mappings":[{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K002-M01","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R010::theta::v141-c-R010-p-Ki","v141-c-R007::theta::v141-c-R007-theta-K_i","v141-c-R003::theta::theta_K_i"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-G01-E20","v141-b-g02-e005"],"rationale":"Both refer to the same prosumer's allowed load category set, used respectively for product, participation, and welfare configuration; not merged with the substitution set."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K002-M02","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R010::x::v141-c-R010-x-zik","v141-c-R007::x::v141-c-R007-x-zik","v141-c-R003::x::var_z_ik"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E14","v141-b-G01-E20"],"rationale":"Both are category load allocation power in the source load constraint, retaining product-use, eligibility-expression, and optimization-decision roles."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K002-M03","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R010::x::v141-c-R010-x-zig","v141-c-R007::x::v141-c-R007-x-zig","v141-c-R003::x::var_z_ig"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E14","v141-b-G01-E20"],"rationale":"Both are grid-category allocation power in the same load constraint; each chain's local role and unit record remain as-is."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K002-M04","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R010::theta::v141-c-R010-p-zpred","v141-c-R007::theta::v141-c-R007-theta-zpred","v141-c-R003::theta::theta_z_pred"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-G01-E20"],"rationale":"The same forecast load input on the right-hand side of the source load constraint is reused across three functional scopes, without rewriting its original fields."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K002-M05","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R010::theta::v141-c-R010-p-Kg","v141-c-R003::theta::theta_K_g"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-G01-E24","v141-b-G01-E25"],"rationale":"Both are sets of energy of allowed categories that is substituted and stored as grid energy; case green energy is not automatically defined as all members of this set."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K002-M06","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R010::x::v141-c-R010-x-bikg","v141-c-R003::x::var_b_ikg"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-G01-E24","v141-b-G01-E25"],"rationale":"Both correspond to source substitution storage quantity, retaining their set conditions and original unit differences, and are not merged with the actually executed optimal reference values."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K002-M07","kind":"alternative_representation","member_refs":["v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C003","v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C002","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C009"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-G01-E20","v141-b-g02-e005"],"rationale":"Both center on source constraints (7)-(8), but R007 additionally writes in set-inclusion relations and has different quantifier wrapping. These alternative representations of same-type constraints are retained; the entire item is not deemed unconditionally replaceable."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K002-M08","kind":"same_expression","member_refs":["v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C002","v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C007"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C002","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e027"],"rationale":"Both express the same procedural permission in this case that subsidized energy is only for low-income households; the representative only resolves display duplication, and the product and participation bindings remain."}],"gaps":[{"gap_id":"v142-d-K002-G01","category":"math_incomplete","description":"The existing load formula only restricts the sum to the allowed category set while giving non-negativity conditions for all categories; it does not explicitly set load allocation for categories outside the set to zero. Therefore, the verbal use eligibility cannot be directly regarded as a fully mathematical prohibition condition.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R007","v141-c-R010","v141-c-R003"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C003","v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C002","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C009"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-G01-E20","v141-b-g02-e005"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Check whether the original text and variable definitions contain another out-of-set prohibition convention; if not, retain this mathematical coverage gap and do not fabricate a zeroing constraint in D."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K002-G02","category":"scope_conflict","description":"The frozen chain does not give the complete correspondence of case category names and numerical indices, per-prosumer allowed sets, and substitution sets. Green premium and low-income subsidy restrictions support only the stated case and cannot be generalized into eligibility rules for arbitrary energy categories or arbitrary regions.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R007","v141-c-R010","v141-c-R003"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C002","v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C005","v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C006","v141-c-R010::theta::v141-c-R010-p-Ki","v141-c-R010::theta::v141-c-R010-p-Kg","v141-c-R003::theta::theta_K_i","v141-c-R003::theta::theta_K_g"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e027","v141-b-g02-e028"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"If an executable case configuration is needed, later supplement source-supported category indices and participant-set correspondences; general rules and case conditions remain separate."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K002-G03","category":"ontology_extension","description":"Energy categories and category-specific subsidy use eligibility can, in the existing framework, only be carried via product and consumer nodes; this cannot be taken to mean that category or eligibility concepts have been approved for addition to the framework.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R007","v141-c-R010"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R007::V::participation.consumer","v141-c-R010::V::product.local_energy"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-G01-E20","v141-b-g02-e027","v141-b-g03-e01"],"proposal_ids":["v141-b-g02-p001","v141-b-g02-p002","v141-b-g03-ext-energy-class"],"required_work":"Manually handle the category and subsidy eligibility proposals and their mutual duplication relations; this round only cites proposal IDs and adds no nodes or eligibility graph edges."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K002-G04","category":"unverified_source","description":"The category, set, and case eligibility bases of this cluster all come from still unreviewed B citations; the mapping only has experimental candidate support eligibility.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R007","v141-c-R010","v141-c-R003"],"object_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-G01-E20","v141-b-G01-E24","v141-b-G01-E25","v141-b-g02-e027"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Manually check set definitions, quantifiers, prohibition conditions, and case scope; the current assembly cannot be interpreted as having passed independent scientific review."}]},"rule_refs":["28-multiclass_prosumer_preferences::v141-c-R010","28-multiclass_prosumer_preferences::v141-c-R007","28-multiclass_prosumer_preferences::v141-c-R003"],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"node_ids":["COMP-7f5e3dcddfa1014c","COMP-ebacec241379c91d","KG40-3bf0b2932a5782b5","KG40-45833afd23977831","KG40-a9ae52fd85070f81"]});
